      {
        "question_text": "Convert $845\\text{ mg}$ to kilograms.",
        "solution_text": "Identify the given unit and the requested unit: milligrams to kilograms.\n\nConvert to a larger unit by dividing by $1000$ for each step: $845\\div1000\\div1000=0.000845$.\n\nState the converted mass with its unit: $845\\text{ mg}=0.000845\\text{ kg}$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Convert $3.18\\text{ kg}$ to grams.",
        "solution_text": "Grams are smaller units than kilograms, so multiply by $1000$.\n\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}3.18\\times1000\\\\&=3180\\end{aligned}$\n\n$3.18\\text{ kg}=3180\\text{ g}$.",
        "equationAlignment": {
          "mode": "continuation"
        }
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Convert $9400\\text{ g}$ to kilograms.",
        "solution_text": "Kilograms are larger units than grams, so divide by $1000$.\n\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}9400\\div1000\\\\&=9.4\\end{aligned}$\n\n$9400\\text{ g}=9.4\\text{ kg}$.",
        "equationAlignment": {
          "mode": "continuation"
        }
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Convert $0.0062\\text{ t}$ to grams.",
        "solution_text": "Tonnes to grams takes two steps to smaller units. Multiply by $1000$ at each step.\n\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]\n\\node (t) at (0,0) {$0.0062\\,\\mathrm{t}$};\n\\node (kg) at (42,0) {$6.2\\,\\mathrm{kg}$};\n\\node (g) at (84,0) {$6200\\,\\mathrm{g}$};\n\\draw[->] (t) -- node[above] {$\\times1000$} (kg);\n\\draw[->] (kg) -- node[above] {$\\times1000$} (g);\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]\n\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}0.0062\\times1000\\times1000\\\\&=6.2\\times1000\\\\&=6200\\end{aligned}$\n\n$0.0062\\text{ t}=6200\\text{ g}$.",
        "equationAlignment": {
          "mode": "continuation"
        }
      }
